  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "A caravan servant abandoned as cannon fodder when zombies attack flees into a cave no zombie will approach and finds a demonic inheritance left by the Gu Master who wiped the local clan and raised the tombstone in the ruins. He awakens his aperture there, raises aptitude from C grade to B grade with a rare Gu from the cave, and after more than eight years reaches rank three, the criterion for the final secret chamber.",
      "chapters": [
        254
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_master"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The final chamber holds a stone slab in which that demonic Gu Master professes himself as Second Zombie King. If a fated individual wishes, they may go to Zhao Ze Mountain as an official disciple and follow him to roam the Southern Border. As the final test he requires the inheritor to kill a thousand people and raise a large zombie army, with set counts of white-hair, black-hair, and green-hair zombies, or one blue-hair zombie in place of that mix. The slab also frames a shared servant background that resonates with Ding Hao.",
      "chapters": [
        254
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "final-chamber-test",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_demonic_path",
        "char_second_zombie_king",
        "loc_zhao_ze_mountain",
        "reg_southern_border",
        "char_ding_hao"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan remembers that Second Zombie King left this inheritance after exterminating the clan on Mu Bei mountain, that Ding Hao inherited it, later became Second Zombie King’s eldest disciple, stayed loyal on the demonic path, and chose to die in Second Zombie King’s place at Yi Tian Mountain.",
      "chapters": [
        255
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "previous-life-memory",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "loc_mu_bei_mountain",
        "loc_yi_tian_mountain"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He also recalls that Second Zombie King had not left behind only one inheritance and had taken in seven to eight disciples in that previous life, with Ding Hao only one of them.",
      "chapters": [
        256
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "other-inheritances",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "A much later stretch places the Mu Bei inheritance as what caused Ding Hao’s rise as an enslavement path Gu Master, and names Second Zombie King a rank five peak stage Gu Master from the Southern Border Zombie Alliance branch.",
      "chapters": [
        965
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "enslavement-path-rise",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_zombie_alliance"
      ]
    }
  ],
